{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>חפר אוכל</b> — it seeks, as though to search the entire earth; it is close to the derivation of חופר גומץ (digging a pit). The meaning is that it is in a high place and seeks its food, like the meaning of כחופר מטמון (as one searching for hidden treasure)."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:18.163399925Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}